From 6111f3f75a7dca3be58abe0128b6f9222d0c577f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alberto L <alberto_leon@seas.harvard.edu>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:33:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(message-wake): ring a handle from a mediator's push
 webhook

A mediator built on didcomm-mediator-credo posts {connectionId, fcmToken}
to one URL for every message it queues for an absent recipient. With
GATEWAY_MEDIATOR_WEBHOOK_SECRET set, POST /mediator-webhook/{secret}
treats that token as a wake handle and wakes it as the gateway's own
trigger DID, so only a handle whose controller allowlisted the gateway
is rung. One wake per handle per GATEWAY_MESSAGE_WAKE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECS
(default 30). Each message wake is interactive and carries its own
collapse id (keyring-msg-<random>), so it does not replace an earlier
notification; approval wakes keep the configured one.

Signed-off-by: Alberto L <alberto_leon@seas.harvard.edu>
